00:05:28.857 --> 00:05:34.177
Microsoft turned on a path that lets one Windows 11 PC read memory in another over U.S.

00:05:34.297 --> 00:05:36.797
before, and that link is worth taking apart.

00:05:37.557 --> 00:05:39.837
Tech Power Ops account is a latency test.

00:05:40.297 --> 00:05:45.277
Remote direct memory access skips the usual copy through the operating system, so a job

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:49.337
Ub can sit on several daisy-chained machines and touch the next machine's memory with

00:05:49.337 --> 00:05:51.137
that CPU mostly out of the way.

00:05:51.777 --> 00:05:54.997
USB 4 is the cable, up to 80GB per second.

00:05:55.637 --> 00:06:00.797
Ethernet can already ride the same cable, and a UDP packet on that Ethernet path is the

00:06:00.797 --> 00:06:02.377
thing Microsoft measured against.

00:06:03.017 --> 00:06:07.897
UDP still wraps the message, queues it, and copies it before the far memory is involved.

00:06:08.517 --> 00:06:11.857
The bet is that the software stack, not the wire, was the weight.

00:06:11.857 --> 00:06:20.777
2 PCs, latency versus message size, RDMA over USB 4 came back in 28-50 microseconds. Ethernet

00:06:20.777 --> 00:06:31.257
over USB 4 with UDP came back in 116-194 microseconds. Fast-end, 28 against 116, slow-end, 50 against

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:38.057
194. The outlet calls that roughly 4 times quicker. A picture of DGX Spark machines tied

00:06:38.057 --> 00:06:43.997
with Ethernet is not this test. So it does not add a number. A short message finishes before an

00:06:43.997 --> 00:06:50.797
80 gigabit pipe is full, which is why the 28-50 microsecond access is what you feel and why the UDP

00:06:50.797 --> 00:06:56.997
band is a stack tax. Stretch the message and the bytes have to occupy that pipe, while the protocol

00:06:56.997 --> 00:07:03.457
gap stays inside the band already measured. Daisy-chained PCs stop being the right fabric when the job is

00:07:03.457 --> 00:07:08.237
limited by how many bytes that 80 gigabit pipe can move, not by the memory access.

00:07:08.877 --> 00:07:14.037
A wider network then finishes the step, and the fourfold latency win no longer decides

00:07:14.037 --> 00:07:14.357
it.

